AiezzaUtils

![CI](https://github.com/Luan-Aiezza/AiezzaUtils/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)
https://img.shields.io/badge/ESLint-4B32C3.svg?style=for-the-badge&logo=ESLint&logoColor=white
![Release](https://github.com/Luan-Aiezza/AiezzaUtils/actions/workflows/release.yml/badge.svg)

AiezzaUtils is a lightweight collection of Swift utilities designed to simplify common development tasks.
It includes helper modules such as email validation, date formatting utilities, and optional SwiftUI UI components.
The package is fully modular, documented, and ready to be imported into any iOS project via Swift Package Manager (SPM).

🔗 Installation (Swift Package Manager)
You can add AiezzaUtils to your project directly through Xcode:
File → Add Packages…
Then enter the URL:
https://github.com/Luan-Aiezza/AiezzaUtils.git
Or add it directly to your Package.swift:
.package(url: "https://github.com/Luan-Aiezza/AiezzaUtils.git", from: "1.0.0")
Then include it inside your target:
.target(
    name: "YourApp",
    dependencies: [
        .product(name: "AiezzaUtils", package: "AiezzaUtils"),
        .product(name: "AiezzaUI", package: "AiezzaUtils") // if using the UI module
    ]
)

🧪 Tests (SwiftTests + UI Tests)
The package includes a growing suite of automated tests using Swift Testing, covering both Core utilities and SwiftUI components.
✔️ CoreUtils Tests
The CoreUtilsTests suite validates:
Email validation rules
Multiple supported email formats
String transformations (trimmed, isNotEmpty)
Safe type casting (safeCast)
Date conversions (timestamp, date(from:))

🧩 UI Tests (SwiftUI Components)
The UI module (AiezzaUI) also contains tests validating:
Correct initialization of AsyncImageView
Placeholder rendering behavior
View state before/after loading asynchronous content

🏷️ Versioning
This project follows Semantic Versioning (SemVer):
MAJOR – breaking changes
MINOR – new features
PATCH – fixes
Latest stable release: 1.0.1

